  {
   "id": "credkit-sqlite-every-handle",
   "class": "credential-kit",
   "status": "active",
   "summary": "Every SQLite handle goes through credkit.SQLDriver: internal/credsql registers the one driver and every sql.Open in store.go and platform/migration.go names it, the read-only opener included. The MCP sql value cap moved from sqlite.Limit on a held connection to a DSN parameter that credsql applies as each connection opens.",
   "why": "A statement's text and bound values are a sink of their own, reads included, so a read-only handle on the bare driver would run a statement carrying a credential and withhold only the row afterwards.",
   "spec_encode_followup": "Press-side: generate store, migration and MCP sql opens against one kit-wrapped driver name, and express the MCP sql value cap as a connection-open setting rather than sqlite.Limit on a held connection.",
