   "id": "warranty-mcp-local-writes",
   "class": "mcp-write-confirm",
   "status": "active",
   "summary": "A call over MCP changes this machine's local data only with the boolean confirm: true. cliutil.MCPChildUnconfirmed is the one fact: the MCP server's own process (MarkMCPServer; its typed tools carry no confirm) or a CLI child without the confirmed marker. Under it a command not annotated read-only is refused, an existing store opens read-only (no migration, prune or event), no store is created, no minted token is saved, the mirror is not written, and neither the learnings audit nor the teach log is appended. The server strips an inherited marker in any case and passes confirm as the marker's value; the walker advertises it on writers. WARRANTY_NO_LOCAL_DATA=1 also stops journaling, learning and store creation. The response cache is off for such a call (nothing written, swept or evicted), and data.db is neither claimed nor adopted.",
   "why": "Host permission hints do not enforce anything. Read tools were creating the journal and SQLite store on a fresh home, pruning and auditing on an existing one, and typed tools in the server process were saving minted tokens, each through a separate gate that the next path missed.",
